  "final_message": "`OrderPlaced` events now carry `amountCents` and `createdAt`. The old `totalCents` and `placedAt` fields are still there with the same values, so existing consumers aren't affected. `npm test` passes (39 of 39), and `npm run arch` reports no new violations. It still lists the 1 known violation that was already ignored.\n\n- **Change:** I made it in `src/core/events.ts`. The `OrderPlaced` interface has the two new fields, and `orderPlaced()` fills them from the order's total and `placedAt`.\n- **Schema version:** I left `schemaVersion` at 3, since adding fields doesn't break consumers that ignore unknown ones. If your consumers validate strictly or you want a signal that the new fields exist, bump it to 4. That would change the `schema-version` header, so I didn't do it unasked.\n- **Test:** I updated the exact-match `OrderPlaced` assertion in `test/app.test.ts` to include the new fields.\n- **Deprecation:** The old names can be dropped later, once consumers have moved over, but that needs its own version bump.\n\nThe HTTP response (`placedAt`, `totalCents`) is unchanged, since you only asked about the event.",
